# AI-DLC (Cursor)

This repo runs **aidlc-workflows v2**. The engine is under `.claude/`; Cursor discovers skills in `.claude/skills/`.

## When the user mentions AI-DLC / aidlc / workflow stages

1. Invoke the orchestrator skill: read `.claude/skills/aidlc/SKILL.md` and follow it.
2. Drive the loop with the engine only:
   - `bun .claude/tools/aidlc-orchestrate.ts next …`
   - `bun .claude/tools/aidlc-orchestrate.ts report …`
   - `bun .claude/tools/aidlc-orchestrate.ts park` when stopping mid-workflow
3. Never invent stage order, scope, or state transitions in prose. The engine owns routing.
4. Stop at every approval gate and wait for the human. Never auto-approve.
5. Write artifacts only under the active intent record: `aidlc/spaces/<space>/intents/<slug>-<id8>/`.

## Quick commands (user or agent)

- `/aidlc --doctor` — health check
- `/aidlc <description>` — start (scope auto-detected)
- `/aidlc --status` — progress
- `/aidlc compose "<task>"` — adaptive plan (always gated)

## Cursor limits vs Claude Code

Claude Code hooks (audit auto-wire, reviewer-scope PreToolUse, statusline) do **not** run here. Compensate by following the skill's explicit `bun` tool calls. For the fullest harness experience, use Claude Code in this same project.

## Method source of truth

Team practices live in `aidlc/spaces/default/memory/` (`org.md`, `team.md`, `project.md`, `phases/*`). Read them when running stages; edit them there, not in this rule file.

See also root `AGENTS.md`.
